				</Value>
				<Value Code="Q21">
					<Title>watt square metre</Title>
					<Description>Unit of the first radiation constants c1 = 2·p·h·c0², the value of which is 3,741 771 18·10?¹6-fold   that of the comparative value of the product of the derived SI unit watt multiplied with the power of the SI base unit metre with the exponent 2.</Description>
				</Value>
				<Value Code="Q22">
